--- a query in a view runs at every render: refused where it is written, by its kind, and sent to a derivation the view reads, as the book teaches (`derive rows`, above the view) — the refusal had sent it to a handler, which is where a write goes
use web, ui, db

book = connect['sqlite://cards.db']

view render[]
    rows = query[book, 'SELECT name FROM cards']
    return p['`len[rows]` cards']

page['/', render]
serve[3100]
